As NATO leaders gather in Ankara tomorrow, Tuesday, the alliance faces a stark test of unity, burden-sharing and strategic clarity, with the war in Ukraine, transatlantic tensions and Middle East instability all pressing heavily on the agenda.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/609109b4-7623-11f1-8dc3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-01T124416Z-395208919-RC2Z4MAG2M50-RTRMADP-3-NATO-SUMMIT-TURKEY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/609109b4-7623-11f1-8dc3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-01T124416Z-395208919-RC2Z4MAG2M50-RTRMADP-3-NATO-SUMMIT-TURKEY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d98fca86-76e5-11f1-b272-03ad2d96f339</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 16:32:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/609109b4-7623-11f1-8dc3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-01T124416Z-395208919-RC2Z4MAG2M50-RTRMADP-3-NATO-SUMMIT-TURKEY.jpg">© Efekan Akyuz / Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's first diagnosed Ebola patient recovers after treatment</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260706-france-s-first-diagnosed-ebola-patient-recovers-after-treatment</link><description>
A French doctor who was the first-ever diagnosed case of Ebola in the country has made a full recovery and has been discharged from hospital.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0d195400-6fe6-11f1-b14c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-29T145943Z-1916668681-RC2XILA0ACED-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-CONGO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0d195400-6fe6-11f1-b14c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-29T145943Z-1916668681-RC2XILA0ACED-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-CONGO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">43821528-7945-11f1-9670-43701cbc316b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 15:31:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0d195400-6fe6-11f1-b14c-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-05-29T145943Z-1916668681-RC2XILA0ACED-RTRMADP-3-HEALTH-EBOLA-CONGO.jpg">© Gradel Muyisa Mumbere/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Major wildfires burn in Southern France as early fire season hits Europe</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260706-major-wildfires-burn-in-southern-france-as-early-fire-season-hits-europe</link><description>
Firefighters are fighting wildfires across southern France and other parts of Europe, and authorities are warning that this year’s fire season has started a month earlier than usual after early heatwaves in May and June left vegetation particularly dry and vulnerable.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e421ecb8-78a2-11f1-94c4-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9AV9GZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e421ecb8-78a2-11f1-94c4-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9AV9GZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bc97419c-791b-11f1-8571-1502fde6b6ee</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 09:30:09 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e421ecb8-78a2-11f1-94c4-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9AV9GZ.jpg">© Matthieu Rondel/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>European football chiefs hit out at Fifa move to lift ban on US star Balgoun</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260706-european-football-chiefs-hit-out-at-fifa-move-to-lift-ban-on-us-star-balgoun</link><description>
European football's governing body Uefa on Monday lashed out at the decision of World Cup organisers Fifa to suspend the immediate one-match ban of the United States striker Folarin Balogun following the intervention of US President Donald Trump.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c91a224a-7948-11f1-8f05-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/world-cupTX2B8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c91a224a-7948-11f1-8f05-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/world-cupTX2B8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c7f02d2e-7943-11f1-8bb1-535b3d18ac61</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 16:19:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c91a224a-7948-11f1-8f05-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/world-cupTX2B8.jpg">AFP - ALFREDO ESTRELLA</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Macron to become first Western European leader to visit post-Assad Syria</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260706-macron-to-become-first-western-european-leader-to-visit-post-assad-syria</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron ​will visit ‌Syria to discuss ways to ​strengthen bilateral ​relations and issues of ⁠mutual interest, ​the Syrian presidency has announced, in what would be the first visit by a Western European head of state since Ahmed al-Sharaa came to power following the overthrow of Bashar al-Assad in late 2024.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4c547388-2b73-11f0-a142-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-05-07T181907Z_891751976_RC26DEA8TI0G_RTRMADP_3_FRANCE-SYRIA.JPG"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4c547388-2b73-11f0-a142-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-05-07T181907Z_891751976_RC26DEA8TI0G_RTRMADP_3_FRANCE-SYRIA.JPG" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7aa4356c-7883-11f1-ae10-d3816765e3bf</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 04:00:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4c547388-2b73-11f0-a142-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2025-05-07T181907Z_891751976_RC26DEA8TI0G_RTRMADP_3_FRANCE-SYRIA.JPG">REUTERS - Stephanie Lecocq</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Rebels seize key-town of Anéfis as rebels tighten grip on northern Mali</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260706-rebels-seize-key-town-of-an%C3%A9fis-as-rebels-tighten-grip-on-northern-mali</link><description>
Tuareg separatists and al-Qaeda affiliates appear to have secured control of a key town in northern Mali following a coordinated offensive by the rebels over the weekend. The Malian army and Russian mercenaries have been holed up in the key camp of Anéfis after the rebels launched their offensive on Saturday 4 July.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/10dcd586-7940-11f1-ad64-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B2HR4MZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/10dcd586-7940-11f1-ad64-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B2HR4MZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f83222f6-792c-11f1-9587-65df0bac37ec</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 17:16:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/10dcd586-7940-11f1-ad64-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B2HR4MZ.jpg">AFP - -</source><dc:creator>Anne-Marie Bissada</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Tour de France bans spectators from third stage as fire burns in French Pyrenees</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260706-tour-de-france-bans-spectators-from-third-stage-as-fire-burns-in-french-pyrenees</link><description>
Spectators have been banned from the third stage of the Tour de France cycling race through the Pyrenees Monday, which will be adapted as a forest fire burns the area.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e1e18bd8-7885-11f1-bb6d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9B677G.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e1e18bd8-7885-11f1-bb6d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9B677G.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b4310ad6-78f5-11f1-a439-11eacdd52a79</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 04:46:50 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e1e18bd8-7885-11f1-bb6d-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9B677G.jpg">© Matthieu Rondel/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Tanzania protesters face heavy security, fear repeat of deadly election violence</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260706-tanzania-protesters-face-heavy-security-fear-repeat-of-deadly-election-violence</link><description>
Tanzanians planning to protest Tuesday against government repression are facing a heavy police presence and warnings from authorities, which recalls the mass killings that followed last October's disputed election.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/730a60f4-7911-11f1-b2ad-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26177707587282.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/730a60f4-7911-11f1-b2ad-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26177707587282.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">682bdc94-7920-11f1-8c90-1502fde6b6ee</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 14:04:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/730a60f4-7911-11f1-b2ad-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26177707587282.jpg">© AP photo</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>England survive Azteca thriller to set up last eight showdown with Norway</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260706-england-survive-azteca-thriller-to-set-up-last-eight-showdown-with-norway</link><description>
England moved into a last eight clash with Norway after they beat Mexico 3-2 in a whirlwind game for the ages at the Estadio Azteca in Mexico City.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/130b0e3c-78ea-11f1-b158-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26187061641672.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/130b0e3c-78ea-11f1-b158-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26187061641672.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e36db15e-78ec-11f1-8cc9-a74e16d03ea6</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 03:52:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/130b0e3c-78ea-11f1-b158-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26187061641672.jpg">AP Photo/Natacha Pisarenko - Natacha Pisarenko</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Haaland's late strikes take Norway past Brazil to last eight for first time</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260705-haaland-s-late-strikes-take-norway-past-brazil-to-last-eight-for-first-time-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Erling Haaland scored twice in the last 11 minutes to sweep Norway past Brazil into the World Cup quarter-finals for the first time.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9b46bd10-78c1-11f1-a718-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Bhaaland9BY7WN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9b46bd10-78c1-11f1-a718-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Bhaaland9BY7WN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">58577796-78b3-11f1-8de9-e9da8b034b41</guid><pubDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 22:52:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9b46bd10-78c1-11f1-a718-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-Bhaaland9BY7WN.jpg">AFP - JEWEL SAMAD</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>Summit host Turkey eyes major weapons deals with NATO allies</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260705-summit-host-turkey-eyes-major-weapons-deals-with-nato-allies</link><description>
Next week's NATO Summit in Ankara is expected to showcase Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan’s rising influence within the alliance, as he aims to use the gathering to overcome resistance to crucial arms deals and highlight the rapid growth of Turkey’s defence industry.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/609109b4-7623-11f1-8dc3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-01T124416Z-395208919-RC2Z4MAG2M50-RTRMADP-3-NATO-SUMMIT-TURKEY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/609109b4-7623-11f1-8dc3-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-01T124416Z-395208919-RC2Z4MAG2M50-RTRMADP-3-NATO-SUMMIT-TURKEY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4003e9e0-76e7-11f1-826d-1d81afdc4925</guid><pubDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 15:18:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dorian Jones</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Three sons of Iran's slain leader Khamenei appear at funeral, not successor Mojtaba</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260705-three-sons-of-iran-s-slain-leader-khamenei-appear-at-funeral-not-his-successor-mojtaba</link><description>
Three sons of slain Iranian leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei prayed beside his coffin and those of four other family members on Sunday, but Mojtaba, the son who has succeeded him as Iran's supreme leader, ​did not make ‌an appearance.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ef8054e8-785f-11f1-a2eb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-05T102559Z-2125512687-RC2M7MAIW1PK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-KHAMENEI.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ef8054e8-785f-11f1-a2eb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-05T102559Z-2125512687-RC2M7MAIW1PK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-KHAMENEI.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3ec282a4-7849-11f1-9c29-79bdaaae159b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 16:07:33 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ef8054e8-785f-11f1-a2eb-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-05T102559Z-2125512687-RC2M7MAIW1PK-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-KHAMENEI.jpg">© Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>World Cup bosses wipe out ban for US striker Balogun on eve of Belgium tie</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260706-world-cup-bosses-wipe-out-red-card-for-us-striker-balogun-on-eve-of-belgium-tie-world-cup-2026</link><description>
World Cup organisers Fifa on Sunday suspended the one-match for Folarin Balogun for his red card during the United States' 2-0 victory in the last 32 over Bosnia and Herzegovina on 1 July.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/96cb3060-78dd-11f1-a72e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/balogun-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/96cb3060-78dd-11f1-a72e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/balogun-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">87497280-78cb-11f1-bb1a-9f650f0f23df</guid><pubDate>Mon, 06 Jul 2026 02:08:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/96cb3060-78dd-11f1-a72e-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/balogun-1.jpg">Getty Images via AFP - JAMIE SQUIRE</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>France's richest man Bernard Arnault ordered to pay €22.5m in back taxes</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260705-france-s-richest-man-bernard-arnault-ordered-to-pay-%E2%82%AC22-5m-in-back-taxes</link><description>
Bernard Arnault, head of the luxury goods group LVMH, has been ordered to pay nearly €22.5 million in back taxes after a Paris appeals court overturned earlier rulings in his favour in a long-running dispute with the tax authorities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5e6345d2-57e3-11ee-aae5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Arnauld%20Diner%20Charles.JPG"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5e6345d2-57e3-11ee-aae5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Arnauld%20Diner%20Charles.JPG" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">be08bdea-786b-11f1-a6cc-d36f21a515ea</guid><pubDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 13:06:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/5e6345d2-57e3-11ee-aae5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Arnauld%20Diner%20Charles.JPG">REUTERS - BENOIT TESSIER</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>From memes to political movement, India's 'Cockroach' party leads youth revolt</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260705-india-cockroach-party-transforms-online-satire-into-youth-revolt-cjp-dipke-protest</link><description>
India's Cockroach Janata Party began life as a series of internet memes and has grown into a real-life movement, bringing together young people angry about unemployment and alleged exam fraud. What began five weeks ago as a satirical response to comments by India's chief justice has become a fast-growing campaign which now has political ambitions, even as observers question whether it can survive without more effective organisation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928ac300-7228-11f1-84c5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6YE6U3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928ac300-7228-11f1-84c5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6YE6U3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ffffa734-746c-11f1-aeba-432894e2c7a6</guid><pubDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 07:30:37 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/928ac300-7228-11f1-84c5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B6YE6U3.jpg">AFP - NARINDER NANU</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>The Afghan women farmers keeping their village alive</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260705-the-afghan-women-farmers-keeping-their-village-alive</link><description>
In a remote province of northeastern Afghanistan, women farmers are playing a vital role in their community's survival among the snow-capped mountains.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/38b8e714-74f6-11f1-8bb9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/5386024510adaba2ebca1dd8274bbd4b1b43328c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/38b8e714-74f6-11f1-8bb9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/5386024510adaba2ebca1dd8274bbd4b1b43328c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4bc522b2-75fc-11f1-a2ba-6157ab31bd8e</guid><pubDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 11:50:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/38b8e714-74f6-11f1-8bb9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/5386024510adaba2ebca1dd8274bbd4b1b43328c.jpg">© Wakil KOHSAR / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Hunger in northern Nigeria reaches worst levels in nearly a decade, WFP says</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260705-hunger-in-northern-nigeria-reaches-worst-levels-in-nearly-decade-united-nations-world-food-programme-says</link><description>
More than 17 million people across nine conflict-hit states in northern Nigeria face severe hunger, the UN's food agency (WFP) has said, warning that violence and funding ‌cuts are driving food insecurity to its worst level in nearly a decade. Stripped of their livelihoods, some people are fleeing across the border into neighbouring Benin.
